From 600b23ae3aaa3044f526cde69c9643bd142b048e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 02:52:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AI_AB_TEST Economy: EarlyStrike book as the expert openings
 (per-civ plan, priorities with conditions, luxury tech, K cities, fallback)

The user: "use the experts ideas right away and we will know if they are
good by if they take cities." Under EarlyStrike (no new flag):
- a per-civ plan (CvPlayer::GetEarlyStrikePlan, CvEarlyStrikePlan): core
  and support classes, siege, N core units before the first settler, core
  and support totals, K cities before the strike, fallback turn (T50
  Quick), first policy tree. Numbers from Personality's strike-plan spec
  for the Huns (core Horse Archer, Rams as siege, K 3), Aztec (the user's,
  K 2), Inca (Slingers, Spearman in front, K 3), Greece and Celts
  (Hoplites / Pictish Warriors with Archers, K 3); other early-spike civs
  keep the user's Aztec opening. Personality's profile fields replace the
  table when they land.
- capital book as priorities with conditions, rebuilt at each choice:
  core units while a barbarian camp or a major's city is within 8 tiles,
  until N; then worker and settler (first, when nothing is in reach);
  then siege, support, the rest of the core; settlers up to K;
- research: spike tech, one luxury tech (only while we have no luxury
  and one next to our cities needs a tech), support tech, the upgrade
  (Personality's eUpgradeTech, else the ranged unit's upgrade within the
  first 4 columns), siege tech; then the warmonger list;
- small empire: no settler built past K cities, none bought before the
  strike; DoHurry and tiles still spend nothing before the strike;
- fallback: past the fallback turn with no target in reach and no war,
  IsEarlyStrikeBook goes false (back to the normal plan);
- first policy tree from the plan (Honor for all five, as 0030).
On claude/ab-c1 db638c3. Written 9:53pm ET.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
